  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the Capacity of the Common Financial Management Platform</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The establishment of the PFMU in Nigeria has assisted in improving accounting, financial management and auditing in the country as well as for donor asssited projects.  The advantages and successes are evident in all states given that they have accepted to institutionalize the unit in their respective financial systems.  The Federal Government has also sent a letter to the Bank requesting for support in this regard.  The IDF will assist in strengthening, consolidating and sustaining the gains recorded both at the federal and state levels. The components are as follows:  - Component 1:  Extension of PFMU Software system in Offices of the Accountant General and Federal Project Financial Management Unit. - Component 2:  Training and Enlightenment Workshop to reinforce capacity. - Component 3:  Audit The objective of the grant is to strengthen the capacity of the Office of the Accountant General of the Federation (OAGF) and the Offices of the Accountant and Auditor General (OAGS &amp; OAuGS) in the 36 States and Federal Capital Territory (FCT) as well as promote accountability and greater use of country systems for donor assisted operations.</narrative>
  </description>
